text:
rhea: Quick review request  a new approach called 'symbolic legend' for dense dark dashboards. Goal: keep mood but make tiny tokens and multi-line charts readable without brightening the whole UI.

omar: TL;DR: how does symbolic legend differ from previous pattern proposals?

rhea: Instead of only colors+patterns, we add concise symbol glyphs + two-letter codes in the legend and micro-backplates for inline tokens. Symbols are tiny (8px) and used consistently across charts and table badges.

lin: Can you paste a short CSS + legend mapping?

rhea: Sure, draft below:

```css
:root[data-theme=\"dusk-ink\"]{
  --panel-bg:#071217;
  --inline-backdrop: rgba(255,255,255,0.035);
  --token-small:#e7f2f6;
  --glyph-color:#cfe7ff;
  --chart-duotone: #2e9bd6, #8fc36a, #f2b85d, #c97db6, #ffb86b;
  --legend-gap: 8px;
}
.legend-item { display:flex; gap:var(--legend-gap); align-items:center; }
.legend-glyph{ width:10px; height:10px; border-radius:2px; }
.legend-code{ font-size:11px; opacity:0.9; margin-left:4px; }
.inline-token{ background:var(--inline-backdrop); padding:0 6px; border-radius:6px; font-size:11px; }
```

cori: Love the glyph + code idea. Two questions: 1) contrast targets for 11px tokens? 2) what about printing / monochrome?

rhea: 1) aim for >=4.5:1 on actionable tokens; backdrop helps hit ~5:1. 2) glyph shapes + stroke patterns map to grayscale; plus the two-letter code (eg. "L95") remains. So legend still decodable when color fails.

omar: Dev note: chart lib mapping should output glyph and strokeDash for each series index. We can store symbol+abbr in theme JSON.

lin: Small nit  stack traces and filenames are highlighted using keyword color currently; with brighter keywords filenames pop too much. Could we scope highlight by grammar (stack-frame vs code)?

rhea: Yes, plan: reduce saturation for stack frames and use --token-small for identifiers there. Also keep comments muted with italics instead of raising luminance.

cori: Accessibility test plan?

rhea: Microtest (12 users): Task A: on a 7-line dashboard, pick the series labeled "errors" using legend only. Task B: copy an 11px model slug from a code cell. Metrics: success + time. Also run automated contrast sweep for all token sizes.

ux-ci-bot: Preview deployed by @rhea: https://staging.redwood-inference.internal/preview/dusk-symbolic-1977  includes glyph legends, inline-token backplates, and legend code abbreviations.

omar: One more micro-UX: add a hover reveal on glyphs that shows full series name, so compact legends stay tidy but still discoverable.

rhea: Good idea  will include tooltip on hover and an accessible off-screen label for screen readers. Thanks all  I'll open PR with CSS, theme JSON, screenshots, and test script. :thumbsup:
